e/godot/pulls/114907","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114907","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114907.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114907.patch","merged_at":"2026-01-13T21:22:56Z"},"body":"Fixes: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113676\r\nThe \"high quality\" mode was mostly fixed by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114279 and this fixes the issue that @BlueCube3310 noted with the fast filter path\r\n\r\nThere were a couple of problems with the fast filter path introduced by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107902:\r\n1. The downsampled radiance map had too many mipmaps leading to the lowest level having really poor quality\r\n2. The fast filter path didn't use the high quality path, so extremely bright pixels had a random chance of bleeding through\r\n3. The Jacobian approximation used the wrong input coordinates, so it wasn't helpful at all\r\n\r\nThis PR looks scary, but most of the code changes are just removing the `DOWNSAMPLER_MODE_FLAG_HIGH_QUALITY` since we should always use the more advanced mipmapping approach (as we did previously). For high frequency skies (like in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114750) it is absolutely necessary. \r\n\r\n_Before_\r\n\r\n<img width=\"640\" height=\"599\" alt=\"Screenshot from 2026-01-12 21-12-42\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/46245638-20dd-48f3-b81e-53dfb04e3f9a\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"640\" height=\"640\" alt=\"fast-filter-before\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/be8d657a-29be-4fdc-b8f1-efef3a34107c\" />\r\n\r\n_After_\r\n\r\n<img width=\"640\" height=\"599\" alt=\"Screenshot from 2026-01-12 21-14-19\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a302002e-83b3-4a11-bca1-bfc3ee793bd6\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"640\" height=\"640\" alt=\"fast-filter-after\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5bc21617-b55c-420e-9198-e2766fd168c7\" />\r\n","closed_by":{"lo